<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<gpx version="1.1" creator="trawsfynydd-cycle-vision research" xmlns="http://www.topografix.com/GPX/1/1">
  <metadata>
    <name>Bala and Festiniog Railway - Blaenau Ffestiniog to Trawsfynydd (disused, mothballed)</name>
    <desc>Concept-stage alignment stitched from OpenStreetMap way data (ODbL). NOT an approved cycle route.</desc>
  </metadata>
  <wpt lat="52.9946" lon="-3.93838">
    <ele>217.0</ele>
    <name>Blaenau Ffestiniog</name>
    <desc>Still an active station today — southern terminus of the Conwy Valley Line (Transport for Wales) and northern terminus of the heritage narrow-gauge Ffestiniog Railway to Porthmadog. The route concept would start from this live station, not a dead site.</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="52.9591" lon="-3.9304">
    <ele>191.0</ele>
    <name>Festiniog (Llan Ffestiniog)</name>
    <desc>Site demolished by 2011; mothballed trackbed runs through the former station site, overgrown. Subject of a 2016-2020 community clearance effort that did not result in reopening.</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="52.9401" lon="-3.9446">
    <ele>185.0</ele>
    <name>Maentwrog Road</name>
    <desc>Station building and stationmaster's house are long-standing private residences. The A470 road bridge immediately north was rebuilt in 2002 in a way that preserved the rail line beneath/beside it.</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="52.9279" lon="-3.9368">
    <ele>216.0</ele>
    <name>Trawsfynydd Lake Halt</name>
    <desc>Platform remains, rediscovered under vegetation by 2017 volunteer clearance; no services since 1960.</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="52.9061" lon="-3.9137">
    <ele>247.0</ele>
    <name>Trawsfynydd</name>
    <desc>Former station building is a private residence; former goods yard/military-camp sidings now in agricultural use. The 1999-era engine shed was last reported standing (used as a store).</desc>
  </wpt>
  <trk>
